name: Recorded imports remain readable without claiming local discovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/httpx-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recon:import httpx imported | httpx
expect: 1 out-of-scope
expect: skipped
expect-not: Scan 2/3
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART httpx
paste-file: @ART/broken-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Earlier saved evidence may remain | partial-import
expect: line 2
expect: Complete import is not claimed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART broken
ask: Does a malformed later record show failure, preserved earlier evidence and the input line without pretending the import completed?
paste-file: @ART/har-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recon:import har imported 1 | har
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART har
paste-file: @ART/bounty-har-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 bounty:import-har imported 1 | compatibility-har
paste-file: @ART/burp-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 bounty:import-burp imported 1 | compatibility-burp
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART final
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: reader-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: reader-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: reader-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: reader-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: reader-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: reader-tail-40x12
keys: PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage
live-snap: reader-page-one-40x12
keys: PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage
live-snap: reader-page-two-40x12
keys: PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage PPage
require-live-snap: 15 Import stopped | reader-page-three-40x12
expect: Earlier saved evidence may remain
expect: Complete import is not claimed
ask: Is imported evidence and the partial-import disclosure reachable at every viewport through the existing transcript reader controls?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 LOGS | reader-back
resize: 120x36
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 imported | review-evidence
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
ask: Are labeled synthetic HTTP requests readable as imported observations while local Map and Scan remain incomplete?
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-required
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART final
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 imported | recovered-evidence
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | recovered-setup
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/recorded_recon.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does restart preserve imported observations and require genuine repository context and discovery without creating provider calls or scan jobs?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
